// tests/quote-request.test.mjs — PUBLIC-QUOTE-REQUEST-SPEC.md §7.6 (WS-B): the pure server logic behind the public
// "Get a quote" flow (functions/qr-core.js) plus the guarantees that matter most:
//
//   * NO PRICE LEAVES THE SERVER. publicEstimate() is the only builder of the qrEstimate response; its key set is pinned
//     EXACTLY, it carries no exact total / line / unit price, and low/high/step are null whenever shown is false.
//   * ONLY PUBLISHED PRODUCTS ARE QUOTABLE. The allowlist (functions/qr-published.json) is GENERATED by
//     scripts/build-catalogue.js from the same walk that decides which cards reach /catalogue/ — never typed by hand — and
//     this file proves it agrees with the committed page, the committed category map, and (when the private master is
//     present) the master itself; exhaust / fresh-air / gas-line / fire-suppression and the 49 excluded items (21 non-equipment + 28 specialised) are refused
//     with the very same message an unknown id gets.
//   * Validation (intake, contact, items), the range + gate wiring, the session counter, the bot check, the LRU, the
//     product-cache policy, the notification text (no `<`, plain emoji, never the exact figure).
//   * ONE PRODUCT, ONE MULTIPLIER (adversarial review): units of a product (qty x runs) are capped across ALL its lines, so
//     duplicate lines cannot turn the rounded range into an exact-price oracle or defeat the minimum-basket gate.
//   * HOSTILE SHAPES: a body whose fields hide on a smuggled __proto__ (firebase-functions' decoder) is refused before it can
//     dodge the payload-size guard or the strict-key allowlists (isPlainJsonTree).
//   * The staff screen and the public page logic, run from their REAL source (vm): hostile text is inert, handlers carry
//     only the server-minted ref, the page's size / unit-cap rules agree with the server's.
//
// PRODUCT FAMILIES (owner ruling 2026-10-21): the SKUs a configurable family absorbs are no longer quotable as plain lines (the allowlist
// lists only the FIXED items); a configured line { familyId, config, dims, qty, note } is validated strictly against the family and priced
// from its primary SKU + the private sheet. The family logic itself is pinned in tests/product-families.test.mjs; here: the allowlist
// semantics, the plain-line refusals, and the page helpers that must agree with the server.
//
// Fixtures are synthetic (round, made-up pesos): the repo is PUBLIC and the real price master is private.
//
// Mutation-tested (scratch copies, never the shared tree; see the commit message for the record): dropping the published
// filter, letting `exact` into publicEstimate, letting a bad mobile through, skipping the Manila date window, removing the
// per-product unit cap (or counting qty only, or off by one), letting the decoder's prototype through isPlainJsonTree,
// relaxing the staff screen's ref guard — and so on; each must fail here.
//
// Run with: node --test tests/*.test.mjs

